# Nechto — agent context

Art-space platform for the Belarus market (Дом Независимого Творца). Monorepo MVP: auth, profiles/avatars, shared contracts, Docker Compose.

Node **>= 22.18**. After package source changes used with Docker bind mounts, run `npm run build:packages` on the host so `dist/` is available.

## Stack

- `apps/web` — Next.js 16 (App Router) + React 19 + Tailwind CSS 4 + TypeScript + next-intl (ru default, en)
- `apps/api` — NestJS 11 + TypeScript (`module`/`moduleResolution`: `nodenext`) + Prisma + Zod env
- `packages/api-contract` — shared Zod request schemas + response types
- `packages/api-client` — typed fetch client used by web
- PostgreSQL 16 via Docker Compose (`prisma migrate deploy` on API start)
- Local run: `docker compose up --build`
- Shared TS: `tsconfig.base.json` (strict); no deprecated `baseUrl` / `moduleResolution: node`

## Layout

```
apps/web                 # frontend (app/[locale], messages/, i18n/, lib/env.ts)
apps/api                 # backend API (prisma/, config/env.ts)
packages/api-contract    # shared API schemas/types
packages/api-client      # shared typed HTTP client
docker-compose.yml
tsconfig.base.json
```

## Agent conventions

- Keep changes scoped; no drive-by refactors
- Prefer TypeScript everywhere (configs included when practical)
- Do not add Kubernetes / LangChain / payments until product needs them
- Verify with `npm run typecheck`, `npm run lint`, and `npm run format:check` when touching shared tooling or many files
- Format with Prettier (`prettier.config.mjs`); do not fight it with manual style diffs
- Auth uses JWT httpOnly cookies + `JwtAuthGuard`; never store passwords in plaintext
- Web session reads (`me` / profile) load in RSC via `lib/session.ts` + cookie forwarding (`lib/api-server.ts`); Docker sets `API_INTERNAL_URL=http://api:3001`
- File uploads go through `StorageService` (local disk); do not write ad-hoc disk or cloud SDK calls in feature modules
- Put request/response contracts in `@nechto/api-contract` and call the API through `@nechto/api-client` from web; rebuild packages after contract changes (`npm run build:packages`)
- Match IDE TypeScript strictness when relevant (CSS side-effect imports need `*.css` module declarations)
- Comments: English only (see `english-comments` rule)
- UI copy: Russian + English via next-intl (see `i18n-bilingual` rule)
- Commits: English Conventional Commits (see `conventional-commits` rule)
- Tests: Jest for API/packages, Playwright for UI; cover new behavior (see `testing` rule)
- Architecture / SOLID: see `architecture-principles`
- File size / extracts: see `file-decomposition` (helpers and hooks in their own files; no mega-modules)
- Web UI decomposition: see `frontend-components` (`components/ui` primitives → features → pages)
- API layering & reliability: see `backend-architecture`
- Before push: see `quality-gate` (no junk, checks green)
- Git: see `git-pr-workflow` (PRs for review; user merges `main`)
